<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21846" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impĕnĕtrābĭlis</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		2. inpenetrabilis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that cannot be penetrated</i>, <i>impenetrable</i> (perh. not ante-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silex ferro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					36, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superior pars corporis crocodili (with dura),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 4, 2 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tergus hippopotami ad scuta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 25, 39, § 95</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">congeries imbribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					36, 54, § 127</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cruppellarii accipiendis ictibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae impenetrabilia quaeque pervia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 12, 35</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>that cannot be
				overcome</i>, <i>unconquerable</i>, <i>unyielding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patet impenetrabilis ille Luctibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					6, 413</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impenetrabilis blanditiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 4 praef.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mens irae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					7, 561</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pudicitia Agrippinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
